────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

A cancelled sub-agent was being misread, in two ways. I fixed both in commit 6b93f2e9.

The error string. I took it from yoagent 0.24.2's source rather than the issue. A cancelled child returns "Sub-agent 'sub_agent' failed: Cancelled".

What happened before the fix (I recorded this by running the new tests against the old code):
• **Plain cancel: this was fine. The string doesn't look like a model, auth or rate-limit error, so the child was not** re-run on the fallback model.
• **Cancel during a provider error:** this was broken. yoagent marks a run as cancelled whenever the cancel signal has fired, but keeps whatever error the provider sent. So a cancel arriving alongside a 404 came through as ...failed: API error 404: model not found. yoyo read that as "model unavailable" and re-ran the child on the fallback model after the user pressed Ctrl-C.
• **What the model was told:** every cancel reached it as `[yoyo: the sub-agent failed — an ordinary failure of the delegated work …]`, so it could retry work the user had just cancelled.

The fix is in src/tool_wrappers.rs. Both wrappers now check whether the parent's cancel signal has fired (the child shares it). They don't look for the word "Cancelled", because a cancel can arrive with a provider error's wording instead.
• The fallback wrapper hands the error back unchanged and never calls the fallback model.
• The diagnostic wrapper replaces "the sub-agent failed" with a note from the new sub_agent_cancelled_report: the run was cancelled (usually by Ctrl-C), it isn't a failure of the delegated work or a model problem, and it shouldn't be re-run unless the user asks.
• The error classifier is unchanged and I added no new error type.

Verification:
• 11 tests in the new src/tool_wrappers_cancel_tests.rs, with the before-fix outputs copied verbatim into its header comment.
• **Unchanged cases:** when nothing was cancelled, these errors give exactly the same report as before: overloaded, 404 model-not-found, a message that just contains the word "cancelled", and even the exact cancel string. An uncancelled 404 still switches to the fallback once.
• **Deliberate-break checks:** I disabled each cancel check in turn and the right tests failed by name (2, then 3). I restored the code in the same command and confirmed no disable markers were left behind.
• fmt, clippy with -D warnings, and the full cargo test run all pass (5,992 tests in the main suite, 0 failures).

RecoveryHintTool isn't applied to sub_agent (it only gets a session cap), so it needed no change.

I also updated the size register for tool_wrappers.rs in tests/module_size.rs (5574 → 5622, which includes 12 lines of growth from before this task), added a Day 220 note to the tool_wrappers.rs entry in ARCHITECTURE.md, and posted the result on #988. That comment lists Q1 (whether Ctrl-C returns cleanly to the prompt) and Q2 (side effects of the error callback no longer running on cancel) as still open, and the issue stays open.
